### Indicator Showcase

- One pointer marks the active tab and glides to the next one: its two ends ride springs, so it lengthens a little on the way and gathers on the new tab, and it never squashes or scales. `indicatorVariant` only changes how it is painted and `indicatorMotion` picks the springs; `pill` is a raised surface behind the item (a thick line before 2026-09-26).
- The five rows share one `v-model`, so a click in any row, or `Next`, moves every pointer at once. Turn the indicator off to see the fallback, where the active item paints its own fill.

