### Best Practices

- Keep `TxTabItem name` values stable, unique, and equal to the values used in `modelValue` / `defaultValue`.
- Prefer `placement="left"` for Dashboard settings and dense admin surfaces; use top/bottom tabs for short secondary switches.
- Use `defaultValue` only when the matching tab is guaranteed to exist. Use `activation` for static uncontrolled examples.
- Do not put long-lived form state only inside inactive panels; inactive tab content is unmounted during switches.
- For panels whose height changes after async data or image load, combine direct measurement (`contentScrollable=false` or `autoHeight`) with `refresh()` after the content settles.
- Keep `nav-right` compact. Move dense actions into `TxDropdownMenu`, `TxPopover`, or `TxDrawer` instead of growing the tab bar.

## API Reference

### TxTabs Props

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|------|
| `modelValue` | `string` | - | Controlled active tab name. Prop-driven changes update the active panel without emitting `change`. |
| `defaultValue` | `string` | - | Initial uncontrolled active tab. It must match a `TxTabItem name`; otherwise no tab is selected. |
| `placement` | `'left' \| 'right' \| 'top' \| 'bottom'` | `'left'` | Navigation placement; invalid values fall back to `left`. |
| `offset` | `number` | `0` | Extra shift (px) of the `line` indicator along the tab axis. Other variants ignore it; `pill` stopped taking it when it became a surface. |
| `navMinWidth` | `number` | `220` | Minimum navigation width for vertical placements. |
| `navMaxWidth` | `number` | `320` | Maximum navigation width for vertical placements. |
| `contentPadding` | `number` | `12` | Padding applied to the main content panel. |
| `contentScrollable` | `boolean` | `true` | Wrap content in an internal scroll container; height animation disables the wrapper for direct measurement. |
| `borderless` | `boolean` | `false` | Remove the outer border and background for embedded layouts. |
| `autoHeight` | `boolean` | `false` | Enable AutoSizer height animation through the default `animation.size` configuration. |
| `autoWidth` | `boolean` | `false` | Enable AutoSizer width animation through the default `animation.size` configuration. |
| `showIndicator` | `boolean` | `true` | Render the active-tab pointer, which is then the only selection highlight: the active item paints no fill of its own. Set to `false` for text-only navigation; the active item falls back to its own `--tx-fill-color` fill. |
| `indicatorVariant` | `'line' \| 'pill' \| 'block' \| 'dot' \| 'outline'` | `'line'` | How the pointer is painted. `line`: a 2px primary rule from icon to text — never shorter than 16px, centred under a shorter label — resting on the nav divider (on the nav's outer edge for `left` / `right`). `pill`: a raised surface behind the whole item, like TxTabBar's `pill` and TxFlatRadio's thumb (a 6px thick line before 2026-09-26). `block`: a 14% primary tint, no shadow. `outline`: an inset 1.5px primary ring. `dot`: a 6px primary dot 4px in from the divider (from the outer edge for `left` / `right`). `line` and `dot` carry a soft primary glow once they land and drop it while they travel. Invalid values fall back to `line`. |
| `indicatorMotion` | `'stretch' \| 'warp' \| 'glide' \| 'snap' \| 'spring'` | `'stretch'` | Variation of the glide the pointer travels on (springs in Technologies): `stretch` lengthens a little on the way and gathers, with no visible overshoot; `spring` damps less and passes the tab once before coming back; `warp` lengthens further; `glide` moves both ends together, a rigid slide that never lengthens; `snap` is quicker, damped harder, and rests first. Invalid values fall back to `stretch`. |
| `indicatorMotionStrength` | `number` | `1` | Scales how far the pointer lengthens on the way (it multiplies the motion's lag, which stops at 0.85); `0` slides it rigidly at its own length. Negative values clamp to `0`. Mirrored on the root as `--tx-tabs-indicator-strength`. |
| `animation` | `TabsAnimation` | - | Per-area animation configuration for size, nav, indicator, and content transitions. |
| `animation.size` | `boolean \| { enabled?; durationMs?; easing? }` | derives from `autoHeight` / `autoWidth` | Enable and configure AutoSizer size animation; defaults to `autoHeightDurationMs` / `autoHeightEasing`. |
| `animation.nav` | `boolean \| { enabled?; durationMs?; easing? }` | enabled, `220ms ease` | Enable and configure nav width/layout transition variables. |
| `animation.indicator` | `boolean \| { enabled?; durationMs?; easing? }` | enabled, `350ms cubic-bezier(...)` | Pointer travel. `durationMs` time-scales the glide's springs (`350` is the reference; below `100` plays as `100`). `easing` no longer shapes travel and only reaches `--tx-tabs-indicator-easing`. `false` / `enabled: false` lands every change in place. |
| `animation.content` | `boolean \| { enabled?; type?; durationMs?; durationRatio?; easing? }` | enabled `zoom`, `180ms ease` | Configure active-panel entry animation. `type` supports `fade`, `slide`, `zoom`, `blur`, `scale`, and `none`; `durationRatio` derives duration from indicator duration. |
| `autoHeightDurationMs` | `number` | `250` | Default size animation duration when `animation.size.durationMs` is omitted. |
| `autoHeightEasing` | `string` | `ease` | Default size animation easing when `animation.size.easing` is omitted. |

### TxTabs Events

| Event | Params | Description |
|------|------|------|
| `update:modelValue` | `value: string` | Emitted when user activation, `defaultValue`, or `activation` changes the active tab in uncontrolled flow. |
| `change` | `value: string` | Mirrors the same active tab name after activation. Prop-driven `modelValue` updates do not emit it. |

### TxTabs Slots

| Slot | Props | Description |
|------|------|------|
| `default` | - | Provide direct `TxTabItem`, optional `TxTabItemGroup`, and optional `TxTabHeader` nodes. Fragments are unwrapped; unrelated nodes are ignored. |
| `nav-right` | - | Render compact controls at the end of the nav bar, commonly used for horizontal tabs. |

### TxTabs Exposed Methods

| Name | Type | Description |
|------|------|------|
| `refresh` | `() => void` | Forward to the internal AutoSizer `refresh()`. |
| `flip` | `(action: () => void \| Promise<void>) => Promise<void>` | Run an action inside the internal AutoSizer FLIP transition when available. |
| `action` | `(fn: (el: HTMLElement \| undefined) => void \| Promise<void>, optionsOrDetect?: any) => Promise<{ changedKeys: string[] } \| any>` | Forward to the internal AutoSizer action helper; falls back to calling `fn(undefined)`. |
| `size` | `() => { width: number; height: number } \| undefined` | Return the latest measured AutoSizer size. |

### TxTabItem Props

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|------|
| `name` | `string` | *required* | Unique tab name used as the active value and lookup key. |
| `iconClass` | `string` | `''` | Optional icon class rendered before the nav label, inside an `inline-flex` box so a glyph class that sizes itself with `width` / `height` (UnoCSS icons) shows in any host. |
| `disabled` | `boolean` | `false` | Block click activation and render a disabled native button. |
| `activation` | `boolean` | `false` | Mark this tab as the uncontrolled default when neither `modelValue` nor `defaultValue` selects a tab. |
| `active` | `boolean` | `false` | Whether the item is active; injected automatically by TxTabs — set manually only when using TxTabItem standalone. |

### TxTabItem Events

| Event | Params | Description |
|------|------|------|
| `click` | - | Emitted by standalone `TxTabItem` when not disabled; `TxTabs` consumes it to update active state. |

### TxTabItem Slots

| Slot | Props | Description |
|------|------|------|
| `default` | - | Active panel content rendered by `TxTabs`. Inactive panels are not mounted. |
| `icon` | - | Custom navigation icon; replaces `iconClass`. |
| `name` | - | Custom navigation label; falls back to the `name` prop. |

### TxTabHeader Props

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|------|
| `node` | `unknown` | - | Active `TxTabItem` VNode passed by `TxTabs`; use `node?.props` defensively. |

### TxTabHeader Slots

| Slot | Props | Description |
|------|------|------|
| `default` | `{ props: { node?: unknown } }` | Sticky content header rendered above the active panel. |

### TxTabItemGroup Props

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|------|
| `name` | `string` | - | Optional group label rendered in the navigation column. |

### TxTabItemGroup Slots

| Slot | Props | Description |
|------|------|------|
| `default` | - | Child `TxTabItem` nodes. The group component itself renders no DOM outside `TxTabs`. |

## Overview

- `modelValue` is the controlled source. Parent-driven `modelValue` updates do not emit `change` or `update:modelValue` again.
- Without `modelValue`, `defaultValue` wins over `activation`. If `defaultValue` does not match a tab, `TxTabs` renders the empty state instead of falling back to `activation`.
- Only `TxTabItem`, `TxTabItemGroup`, and `TxTabHeader` nodes are collected from the default slot; fragments are supported, arbitrary wrappers are ignored.
- `TxTabItemGroup` is a navigation grouping marker; panel content still comes from each child `TxTabItem`.
- `showIndicator=false` removes the pointer DOM and pointer animation work, and the active item falls back to its own `--tx-fill-color` fill. While a pointer is shown it is the only highlight: the active item drops its fill (on hover too) and changes only its ink. Size animation still observes content/nav when enabled.
- The pointer is `.tx-tabs__pointer > .tx-tabs__pointer-inner`, an absolutely positioned child of the tablist, so it scrolls with an overflowing row. The inner element carries `.is-moving` while it travels, which hides the `line` / `dot` glow — a radial pool of the primary colour reaching 4–5px past the mark at 45% opacity — until it fades back over 0.4s after landing. The root keeps `tx-tabs--indicator-<variant>`, `tx-tabs--motion-<motion>` and the `-hidden` / `-pending` / `-visible` / `-anim` state classes.
- Geometry is measured, not assumed: `line` is inset by the active item's computed padding and the box variants take its computed `border-radius`, so hosts that restyle `.tx-tab-item` keep a matching indicator. A label narrower than 16px still gets a 16px `line`, centred under it. For `top` / `bottom` the tablist fills the bar's height with its items centred, so `line` stays on the divider when `nav-right` content or a host `min-height` makes the bar taller.
- The first measurement lands the pointer in place and fades it in, including when the active tab comes from `modelValue`, `defaultValue` or `activation` — no click is needed to bring it out. It is held at `opacity: 0` until the active tab has a non-zero box, and the root carries `tx-tabs--indicator-pending` for exactly that window. An active tab that later measures 0×0 (the tabs sit in a container that was hidden) hides the pointer until the next real measurement lands it again.
- A click, an arrow key, a parent `modelValue` change, and a change of `indicatorVariant` / `placement` / `offset` glide the pointer to its new box. The end facing the target leads and the trailing end follows on a slower spring, so the pointer lengthens a little on the way and gathers as it lands; across the travel its position and size ride the leading spring, so a variant change reshapes it on the way. It never squashes, stretches or scales. `left` / `right` glide on the vertical axis, with the top and bottom ends in place of left and right.
- A resize (the panel's and nav's `ResizeObserver`) and turning `showIndicator` back on land in place; a resize during a trip only retargets it. `animation.indicator: false` (or `enabled: false`) lands every change and skips the fade-in. Under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` every change lands too, and the fade-in and glow transitions are cut.
- Height animation removes the internal scroll wrapper so AutoSizer can measure panel height directly; use `contentScrollable=false` for manual direct-measurement layouts.
- Inactive tab panels are not mounted. Store persistent panel state outside the panel subtree when it must survive switching.

## Technologies

- Reviewed against `packages/tuffex/packages/components/src/tabs/src/TxTabs.vue`, `TxTabItem.vue`, `TxTabHeader.vue`, `TxTabItemGroup.vue`, and `types.ts`.
- `indicatorMotionStrength` is a runtime prop on `TxTabs` and is now present in the exported `TabsProps` interface.
- `TxTabItemGroup.vue` intentionally renders an empty template; `TxTabs` reads its child `TxTabItem` VNodes and creates the group DOM.
- `TxTabs` filters the default slot by component name, so docs should not show arbitrary wrapper components around tab items.
- **Pointer engine:** `useJellyIndicator` (`packages/tuffex/packages/utils/use-jelly-indicator.ts`), lifted out of TxRadioGroup's button indicator, on its `glide` material. TxTabs passes `springSteps` (`packages/tuffex/packages/components/src/liquid/src/spring.ts`, 1/240 s substeps: the library's frame spring) as the engine's `integrate`, because utils cannot import from components. The glide's defaults (`GLIDE`) and `timeScaleSpring` live in `packages/tuffex/packages/utils/animation/jelly.ts`, beside Radio's jelly material. TxTabs only measures — the active item in the tablist's own coordinates, scroll offset included, normalised against an ancestor transform — and hands the variant's target box to `moveTo()`. The `requestAnimationFrame` loop runs only while the pointer moves.
- **Imperative paint:** the engine's `onFrame` writes `opacity`, `width`, `height` and `transform: translate3d(…) scale(…)` straight onto `.tx-tabs__pointer`; on the glide the scale is always `1.000`. The render function reads none of the engine's state, so a trip never re-renders the tab slots, and no CSS transition touches the geometry — only the fade-in's `opacity`.
- **Switch timing:** a click or a parent `modelValue` change sends the pointer in the tick after the switch renders, from inside the size-animation wrapper rather than once it resolves. With `autoHeight` / `autoWidth` / `animation.size` that wrapper is TxAutoSizer's FLIP, which resolves a frame or more later; waiting for it let the new panel's layout refresh reach the engine first with `animate: false`, which lands, so size-animated tabs jumped instead of travelling. Hiding the pointer calls `moveTo(null)`, so no frame loop outlives it.
- **Motion mapping:** each `indicatorMotion` is a row of `MOTION_GLIDE` — the leading end's stiffness / damping, then the lag: `stretch` 420 / 38 / 0.45, `spring` 420 / 24 / 0.3, `warp` 420 / 38 / 0.7, `glide` 380 / 38 / 0, `snap` 720 / 50 / 0.25. The trailing end rides the same spring played `1 − lag / 2` as fast (0.775× for `stretch`), so it falls behind and catches up; a lag of 0 puts both ends on one spring. `timeScaleSpring(…, durationMs, 350)` plays the springs faster or slower with their damping ratio kept (under 100ms plays as 100ms), so a longer `durationMs` is the same glide, only slower; `indicatorMotionStrength` multiplies the lag (capped at 0.85). Measured on a 100px trip of a 60px `line`: `stretch` reaches about 74px and rests in about 0.45s, `warp` about 84px, `spring` passes the target once by about 9px, `snap` rests first (about 0.32s), `glide` stays 60px. The tablist clips its overflow, so the engine also gets `bounds` — the tablist's scrollable extent along the travel — and an end that would leave it stops at that wall; a `spring` pill 8px from the edge would otherwise reach 1px past it.
- **2026-09-26 change:** the five `tx-tabs-pointer-*` keyframe motions, the CSS transitions on the pointer's geometry and the timer-toggled glow class were replaced by the shared spring. `pill` went from a 6px line to a raised surface, `outline` from a border to an inset ring, `block` lost its shadow, and `line` went from a 3px bar across the middle 60% of the item to a 2px rule from icon to text, never shorter than 16px. The glow, which had sat blurred behind every variant and faded in over a second once a timer fired, became a tight radial pool under `line` / `dot` only. Under an indicator the active item stopped painting a fill, and `iconClass` icons got an `inline-flex` box to size in (an inline `<i>` ignores the glyph class's `width` / `height` and had measured 0×0).
- **2026-09-26, same day — jelly → glide:** the pointer first moved onto Radio's jelly material, which was rejected in review: 不够丝滑、简单 (not silky, not simple). The tabs family — TxTabs, TxTabBar, TxFlatRadio, TxSidebarNav — now rides the glide material, and those four hosts no longer pass `maxGrowth` or `deform`; Radio keeps the jelly.
- **Fixed with it:** the pointer slid in from the nav's top-left corner on first paint and replayed a keyframe on mount; arrow keys moved it only when the panel's ResizeObserver happened to re-measure; four of the five keyframes were cut short by the timer that removed their class at `durationMs`.
- **Rejected alternative:** keeping a keyframe per motion. `warp`, `snap` and `spring` were multi-stop `@keyframes` with an overshooting bezier on every segment, which reverses velocity at each keyframe boundary and reads as jitter at any amplitude (component-guidelines, "State motion"). The five names survive as variations of the glide instead.
- **Rejected alternative:** Radio's jelly for the tabs family. Its phases are discrete uniform scales — a 1.06 × 1.08 ≈ 1.145 pop as a trip starts, a 0.97 thud as it lands — and its stretch saturates with speed (−21% along the travel, +36% across it), so the shape jumped from frame to frame instead of flowing, and a tab pill turned into a tall capsule mid-trip. `maxGrowth` and `deform` capped the amplitude, never the discontinuities. The glide changes only position and size, and both continuously.

- Component sources: `packages/tuffex/packages/components/src/tabs/src/TxTabs.vue`, `TxTabItem.vue`, `TxTabHeader.vue`, and `TxTabItemGroup.vue`.
- Types: `packages/tuffex/packages/components/src/tabs/src/types.ts`.
- **Verified coverage:** `packages/tuffex/packages/components/src/tabs/__tests__/tabs.test.ts` (48 cases) covers activation rendering, enabled and disabled switching, controlled updates, fragments, async tab items, groups, content-animation variants, hidden indicators, visual-prop normalization, exposed AutoSizer methods, tablist ARIA and arrow-key navigation, and that the indicator reveals on first layout while staying hidden until a real measurement exists. On the glide (fake timers, stubbed layout) it checks that the first measurement lands in place on the divider; where `line`, `dot` and the box variants rest in all four placements; the 16px `line` minimum, `offset`, and measuring through an ancestor transform; a click gliding between the tabs, running longer than it starts or ends without ever scaling, and settling exactly on the target, including a click and a parent `modelValue` change while a size animation holds the switch across frames; arrow keys moving the pointer; a variant change reshaping on the way; `.is-moving` only while travelling; the `spring` overshoot stopped exactly at the clipping tablist's edge; `animation.indicator: false` and reduced motion landing without travel; hiding mid-trip, then showing, landing in place; each `indicatorMotion`'s profile (`glide` never lengthens, `warp` lengthens more than `stretch`, only `spring` passes the target, once, and `snap` rests first); `durationMs` time-scaling the trip without changing how far it lengthens; and `indicatorMotionStrength` scaling the lengthening, with `0` a rigid slide. Source contracts pin the single-highlight rule, the absence of pointer keyframes and CSS-eased geometry, and the icon's `inline-flex` box; on the compiled sheet, every pointer transition has a reduced-motion rule repeating its exact selector (a shorter one loses on specificity, which had left the glow's fade running).

