## Customization

| Theme token / CSS variable | Used for |
|----------------------------|----------|
| `--tx-border-color` | Outer border and placement-specific nav divider; the `line` indicator rests on the divider. |
| `--tx-bg-color` | Tabs container background. |
| `--tx-fill-color` / `--tx-fill-color-light` | Inactive item hover surface (`-light`); the active item's own fill (`--tx-fill-color`), shown only when `showIndicator` is `false`. |
| `--tx-color-primary` | `line` / `dot` fill and their glow once landed, the `block` tint (14%), the `outline` ring (60%), the active icon under those four variants, and demo accent fills. |
| `--tx-surface-raised` / `--tx-elevation-1` / `--tx-border-color-lighter` | The `pill` surface (falling back to `--tx-bg-color-overlay`), its shadow, and its inset 1px ring. |
| `--tx-text-color-primary` / `--tx-text-color-regular` / `--tx-text-color-secondary` | Active label and icon (`primary`; colour only, no weight change), resting label (`regular`), resting icon, group labels and empty-state text (`secondary`). |
| `--tx-tab-item-ink` / `--tx-tab-item-icon-ink` | Label and icon ink, set on `.tx-tab-item`. The active state and the indicator variants switch these instead of restyling the children, so a host that recolours `.tx-tab-item__name` under a class of its own still wins. |
| `--tx-tabs-indicator-duration` / `--tx-tabs-indicator-easing` / `--tx-tabs-indicator-strength` | Still generated from the indicator props for hosts to read. TxTabs' own styles no longer use them: the engine takes the duration and strength directly, and the easing no longer shapes travel. |
| `--tx-tabs-content-duration` / `--tx-tabs-content-easing` | Runtime variables generated from content animation props. |
| `--tx-tabs-nav-duration` / `--tx-tabs-nav-easing` | Runtime variables generated from nav animation props. |
